---
import Split from './Split.astro';
---
<section id="how" data-tone="light" class="band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>How I work</h1>
    <div class="g" style="row-gap:40px;margin-bottom:clamp(40px,5vw,72px)">
      <p class="eyebrow" style="grid-column:1/4">My approach</p>
      <Split as="h2" class="h-section" style="grid-column:4/12" text="I build what I design." />
    </div>
    <div class="principles">
      <div class="principle rv"><h3>On the desk</h3><p>On Fusion, portfolio managers needed to explain their numbers to other people. Knowing where a figure came from mattered as much as reading it quickly. I test ideas with the people doing the work, then use prototypes to work through the details with product and engineering.</p><a href="/about">About me</a></div>
      <div class="principle rv"><h3>At home</h3><p>Winking Star started at bedtime. Two adults were trying to remember which routines our two children had finished. I built a shared board where the children earn stars and help a pet grow. We use it at home, and other families can use it on the web or iOS.</p><a href="/winking-star">Winking Star</a></div>
    </div>
    <p class="writing-note">Writing code with AI changed what I could try for myself and what I needed to learn from engineers. I wrote about those first two months in <a href="/writing/when-everyone-can-ship">When everyone can ship</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
#how{padding-top:clamp(112px,12vw,172px)}
#how h1{margin:0 0 clamp(40px,6vw,88px);font:500 clamp(52px,7vw,104px)/1.04 var(--display);letter-spacing:-.035em}
@media(min-width:761px){.principles{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));max-width:68rem}.principle{grid-column:auto}}
.writing-note{max-width:62ch;margin:clamp(28px,4vw,48px) 0 0;color:var(--fg-2);line-height:1.65;text-wrap:pretty}
.writing-note a{color:var(--fg);text-underline-offset:3px}
</style>
